in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl
in @mirror/data

# @mirror/data/text — raw text as a data-grammar lens.
#
# THE TRIVIAL SPECIES under @mirror/data. The lens-onto-bytes shape
# where the carrier IS the wire format: parse and emit are identity
# over the substrate's native `text` type.
#
# === Why this lands as a species ===
#
# The family-root discipline (per `shards/mirror/data.mirror`) is
# that every byte-sourced data input is a `@mirror/data/X` lens.
# Without a `text` species, consumers dispatching over file
# extensions in T19's pretty-printer cascade would have to special-
# case the bare-text fallback (`.md`, `.txt`, unknown extension) as
# an escape from the family — and the cross-cutting discipline
# (carrier-as-section, parse-as-focus, emit-as-settle, idempotence-
# on-roundtrip) would have to be re-justified for every unstructured
# format. Landing `text` as a species closes the family over the
# trivial case: T19 can dispatch `.txt` to `@mirror/data/text`
# without leaving the family.
#
# Per the convergence: the trivial lens IS still a lens. The
# identity functor is a functor; the empty product is a product;
# the trivial carrier is a carrier. The family is closed over the
# minimum case because the discipline requires it.
#
# === The carrier ===
#
# `text` — the substrate's native UTF-8 byte sequence type (per
# shards/glass.mirror's text vocabulary; per boot/std's pervasive
# `text` use). No carrier transformation; no structural shape;
# just bytes-as-text.
#
# === Lens reading ===
#
# parse(text) -> text is the identity projection at the data
# altitude (bytes → bytes, typed as text on both sides);
# emit(text) -> text is the identity projection in the other
# direction. The composition emit ∘ parse IS literally the
# identity on text — the strongest form of the round-trip
# idempotence law that structured species satisfy only modulo
# format ambiguity.
#
# This is structurally equivalent to JSON's parse/emit when the
# json carrier is `string(text)` — the unwrapping is trivial but
# typed. The species exists to surface that triviality as a named
# lens, so consumers can dispatch over `@mirror/data` species
# uniformly.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   identity      The identity morphism on a category's object,
#   morphism      universal across all of category theory
#                 (Eilenberg/Mac Lane 1945). Every lens family
#                 contains an identity lens; this is it for
#                 @mirror/data.
#   text-as-      Plain ASCII / UTF-8 byte streams as the universal
#   substrate     interchange substrate; predates structured
#                 formats. The substrate's text type IS this
#                 historical baseline.
#
# Spec context: docs/research/2026-06-07-pretty-printer-LRM.md
#               (the cascade T19 dispatch-over-extension that
#               pulls @mirror/data/text for the fallback case).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]].
# Substrate recognitions: [[feedback-substrate-pull]],
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]
#                      (bodies forward-promised; the identity body
#                      is mechanically obvious but lands when a
#                      consumer pulls).
# Related shards: data.mirror (the family root above),
#                 data/json.mirror (the canonical structured sibling),
#                 data/yaml.mirror (sibling — structured data),
#                 data/toml.mirror (sibling — structured data).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/mirror/data/text.mirror`
# declares `@mirror/data/text` and only that.

# === parse — bytes → text ===
#
# Identity projection. Body forward-promised per consumer-pull
# discipline; lands as the trivial `fn(t) t` when T19's dispatch
# pulls.
parse(text) -> text { \ }

# === emit — text → bytes ===
#
# Identity projection in the other direction. Body forward-promised.
emit(text) -> text { \ }

out @mirror/data/text
out parse
out emit
